CNN compponents -
Convolution layer
Pooling layer

Convolution - 
A sliding window function (also called a kernel) applied to an input matrix.
A convolution result is called a Feature Map.
A convolutional layer is a stack of feature maps of same size. Each feature map has different parameters which menas they extract different info from input image.

Pooling - Subsample the output of convolutional layers by using a filter. In pooling layer, the filter does not have weights; it just applies an aggregation function (max, sum or avg).













